task.statement:
This tag-normalizer works, but it's an accumulate-into-a-list loop straight out of Java. In Python, a filter-and-transform over a sequence is one expression.

    def clean_tags(raw_tags):
        cleaned = []
        for raw in raw_tags:
            tag = raw.strip().lower()
            if tag != "":
                cleaned.append(tag)
        return cleaned

Rewrite it idiomatically in solution.py; same name, same behavior. (Hint: this is a single list comprehension — no explicit append, no accumulator.)
